Context from prior work:
Goal: Set up the initial Bun-based CLI skeleton for TaskForge with a clear command surface and basic argument parsing so future tasks can plug into a stable entrypoint.
Decisions: Use Bun as the runtime/bin entrypoint; Implement a lightweight, hand-rolled parser isolated from command execution (parser in its own module); Define a command registry interface (name, description, args/options schema, handler) and dispatch against it; Support top-level commands plus global flags --help and --version; Use stdout for normal output, stderr for errors, and explicit non-zero exit codes for failures
Risks: Hand-rolled parser may become brittle as options/subcommands grow; Initial command interface might constrain adding nested subcommands or shared global flags; Bun-specific bin/runtime behavior could differ across dev/CI environments
